ling to further education (adaptability). So concerns.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but regarded as arrogant (crew), relatively weak leadership (crew), also arrogant may affect communication. So mixed.\n\nWe need to compare. Which candidate has strongest overall fit? Candidate C has reliability and decision quality and crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be serious. Candidate B has stress and conscientiousness but uncooperative. Candidate A has anticipation and leadership but unorganized and poor criticism. Candidate D has problem solving and responsibility but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nProbably Candidate C seems strongest overall: reliability, decision quality, crew atmosphere, but communication issues could be mitigated? However egocentric and unwilling to further education are concerns for safety-critical role. Candidate B's uncooperative is also serious. Candidate A's unorganized may affect reliability. Candidate D's arrogance and weak leadership may affect crew.\n\nThus maybe Candidate C is best despite communication issues, because reliability and decision quality are critical. Let's propose recommendation for Candidate C, but note concerns.\n\nWe haven't discussed any candidate yet, but we can start with Candidate C. Provide reasoning and vote.\n\nPUBLIC_MESSAGE: state recommendation for Candidate C, reference that we have not yet discussed others, but based on reliability and decision quality, etc.\n\nMETADATA_JSON vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
